  "notes": [
    "Hellwarden chest combines torso, gorget and pauldrons; legs combine hips and cuisses because the production slots have no neck/shoulder/waist slots.",
    "Imp shackles contain wrist and ankle cuffs in one authored mesh; hands is their primary equipment slot. Spiked collar is upper-body armor in chest.",
    "Skeleton greaves are one shared item for Skeleton_A and Skeleton_B.",
    "Body, Hellwarden_Skull, and Puglin_Tusks are anatomy, not items; Lycan has no removable equipment.",
    "All source weapons are rigidly weighted to hand_r; static equipped meshes are inverse(shared default right_hand_one_hand) * source inverse-bind * source vertices. Identity GripPoint_Primary then shared socket reproduces original authored hand-relative fit.",
    "Weapon values are provisional content balance; armor currently has no invented stat modifiers, matching existing clothing definitions."
  ]
}
